{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (complete; investigation only)\n\nOBSERVATION\nThe described perturbation removes both identity guards from a previously bound local/Jira pair: the binding-store entry and the Jira `rebar-id:<local_id>` label. The next pass creates one inbound local duplicate and one outbound Jira duplicate, then converges once the new entities are labelled/bound.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nTwo independent create arms fire in one reconcile pass. Inbound: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py:compute_binding_walk_mutations` considers every unbound snapshot key; `_adopt_stands_down` returns `False` when `_marked_local_ids(fields)` is empty, so the unlabelled original Jira issue is treated as Jira-native and emits an ADOPT create mutation. Outbound: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py:compute_outbound_mutations` chooses create solely when `binding_store.get_jira_key(local_id) is None`; `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py:create_one` dedups only with JQL `labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"`, which misses after label loss, then creates a new Jira issue and writes label/entity-property/binding.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nConfirmed with a bounded in-process harness using fake binding store/client and no production Jira. For an unbound local `loc-1` plus unbound Jira snapshot `DIG-1` with no labels, `compute_binding_walk_mutations` returned `adopted ['DIG-1']` and an inbound create mutation. The same pass's outbound differ returned a create mutation for `loc-1`; `create_one` searched exactly `labels = \"rebar-id:loc-1\"`, got no hits, created one Jira issue, added `rebar-id:loc-1`, set entity property `local_id=loc-1`, and `bind_confirm`ed it. This would have been disproven if either arm had used a third identity signal (for example Jira entity property) or if the outbound create branch considered more than binding+label.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nEither explicitly accept and pin the bounded +1/+1 behavior, or add a third durable identity check before outbound create/inbound adopt (most naturally reading the existing Jira `local_id` entity property) so simultaneous loss of binding+label still reconnects instead of duplicating."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788737395089398001,"uuid":"25d570c6-aa61-4148-8a6c-7f8ccd7ee81d"}